  "limitations": [
    "Local x86_64 Linux native execution with existing cache; new remote ARM64 history job remains a separate CI gate.",
    "Original owner and isolated test signing issuer; no production issuer, Operations dispatch/effect reconciliation, model turn, device effect, historical run resume or kernel G1/G2 qualification.",
    "Lost-response case uses the original-protocol harness; it does not execute a lost-response hepta-submit CLI case.",
    "Actual hepta-submit postpublication result is submit_unknown/objective_owner_request_rejected with a matching compiled publication and null RunStatus. CapacityExceeded is a fixed-source/default-capacity inference; its specific original error bytes were not captured.",
    "Two storage faults are injected after a confirmed controlled owner stop. Byte recovery is established; a mid-write crash or power-loss event is not.",
    "A retained anchor detects missing covered history after reopen in these cases; caller-anchor co-rollback and live disk re-reading are not established.",
    "Historical publication and Unknown do not establish current authorization, execution, success, or a safe retry.",
    "Existing scoped owner suites ran at ee0/d1 before final Box/fmt; this actual runtime uses final 2be source and does not relabel those 307 unit tests as rerun at final head."
